libgvc: don't dereference a NULL active_profile in update_card()

pipewire-pulse can serialize a card to the pulse client before its
SPA_PARAM_EnumProfile params have landed, producing a card with
n_profiles == 0. libpulse resolves pa_card_info.active_profile by matching
the active profile name against the profiles array, so with no profiles the
field stays NULL — and update_card() dereferenced it unconditionally,
killing the whole Wayland session.

On epimetheus this fired on ~2 of 8 graphical boots. pipewire logs
"card N port 0 profiles inconsistent (0 < M)" 0.5-2.2 ms before the fault,
and the kernel reports "segfault at 0", i.e. a literal NULL deref.

The guarded call was always a no-op in this case anyway:
gvc_mixer_card_set_profile() opens with
g_return_val_if_fail (card->priv->profiles != NULL, FALSE), and with zero
profiles that list is NULL. The crash happened purely because the argument
is evaluated before the callee's guard runs.

This is upstream MR !38 verbatim, against issue #47:
  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libgnome-volume-control/-/issues/47
  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libgnome-volume-control/-/merge_requests/38

Kept byte-identical to upstream on purpose. When !38 merges, this stops
applying and the build fails loudly — that is the signal to delete it,
rather than silently carrying a stale delta behind a version check.
homelab.services.upstreamPatchWatch also pings Gotify when the MR changes
state, so we hear about it before a build breaks.

--- a/subprojects/gvc/gvc-mixer-control.c
+++ b/subprojects/gvc/gvc-mixer-control.c
@@ -2646,7 +2646,8 @@
         gvc_mixer_card_set_profiles (card, profile_list);
         gvc_mixer_card_set_name (card, pa_proplist_gets (info->proplist, "device.description"));
         gvc_mixer_card_set_icon_name (card, pa_proplist_gets (info->proplist, "device.icon_name"));
-        gvc_mixer_card_set_profile (card, info->active_profile->name);
+        if (info->active_profile != NULL)
+                gvc_mixer_card_set_profile (card, info->active_profile->name);

         if (is_new) {
                 g_hash_table_insert (control->priv->cards,
